  "tempo": 1.12,
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Those brushes on the side of an escalator are not there to clean your shoes. They're",
      "start": 0.065,
      "end": 3.939
    },
    {
      "text": "warning you.",
      "start": 3.939,
      "end": 4.51
    },
    {
      "text": "The dangerous part is the tiny gap between the moving steps and the stationary side",
      "start": 4.784,
      "end": 9.088
    },
    {
      "text": "panel.",
      "start": 9.088,
      "end": 9.374
    },
    {
      "text": "Loose shoelaces, clothes, or bags can get caught there,",
      "start": 9.76,
      "end": 12.706
    },
    {
      "text": "so the brushes touch your shoes and naturally encourage you to move your feet",
      "start": 13.059,
      "end": 16.631
    },
    {
      "text": "away from the edge.",
      "start": 16.631,
      "end": 17.381
    },
    {
      "text": "Basically, every time you rub your shoe against one because it feels nice,",
      "start": 17.685,
      "end": 21.416
    },
    {
      "text": "the escalator is politely asking you to stop standing next to the part that can",
      "start": 21.727,
      "end": 25.566
    },
    {
      "text": "eat it.",
      "start": 25.566,
      "end": 25.888
    }
  ],
